revert draft on close? Keep the draft when closed (nicer). Actually if you close and reopen, keeping the draft is fine.

Styles: reuse the sidebar-note's tokens and class names but prefix `acryl-hnote-`. Panel classes: `position: fixed; z-index: 30;` plus the applied left/top from the hook. Width 340px, max-width calc(100vw - 24px), max-height 60vh, border-radius 12, background var(--dsw-specific-menu), box-shadow var(--dsw-elevation-prominent), display flex column, overflow hidden.

Now, does the header have `z-index` / stacking that could put the portal above? Portal to document.body with z-index 30 — the sidebar-note used z-index 30 for its panel inside the sidebar (which has its own stacking). For the header, the portal is at body level; other overlays like modals may have higher z-index. Let me check what z-index the app uses for popovers, e.g. the settings modal or tooltip layer. Let me grep the tokens/styles for z-index values.

Actually, to be safe, use a higher z-index like 200? But then it could cover legitimately-higher layers like a modal. The notes panel is opened by a user click and dismissed by outside pointerdown; if a modal is open, the panel would be behind... it can't be open at the same time realistically. Let me check what values are used in the app for menus/popovers.

